I cannot find information about **ai.pharos.xyz** in the docs, so I can’t confirm what that site is.

If you mean Pharos’s AI-connected blockchain tool, the docs cover **Pharos MCP**. It connects AI clients such as Claude Desktop, Cursor, Windsurf, and Codex to Pharos chain data and operations. To get started, add this server to your MCP client configuration:

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "pharos": {
      "type": "http",
      "url": "https://mcp.pharos.xyz/mcp"
    }
  }
}
```

No API key is required. The hosted server is public and limited to 120 requests per minute per IP. See [Pharos MCP](https://docs.pharos.xyz/tooling-and-infrastructure/mcp) for setup details and available tools.

The hosted MCP endpoint is **`https://mcp.pharos.xyz/mcp`**. It uses Streamable HTTP and requires no API key.

Add this server entry in Claude or Cursor’s MCP configuration:

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "pharos": {
      "type": "http",
      "url": "https://mcp.pharos.xyz/mcp"
    }
  }
}
```

If your client only supports `stdio`, use the `mcp-remote` bridge instead:

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "pharos": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "mcp-remote", "https://mcp.pharos.xyz/mcp"]
    }
  }
}
```

See [Pharos MCP](https://docs.pharos.xyz/tooling-and-infrastructure/mcp).

`eth_call` takes a transaction call object and a block number or tag. The call object can include `from`, `to`, `gas`, `gasPrice`, `value`, and `data`. The block defaults to `latest` if omitted.

```json
{
  "to": "0x4100000000000000000000000000000000000000",
  "data": "0x76671808"
}
```

As a JSON-RPC request, the arguments look like this:

```json
{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "method": "eth_call",
  "params": [
    {
      "to": "0x4100000000000000000000000000000000000000",
      "data": "0x76671808"
    },
    "latest"
  ],
  "id": 1
}
```

See [Pharos MCP](https://docs.pharos.xyz/tooling-and-infrastructure/mcp) for the tool overview and [JSON-RPC API Methods](https://docs.pharos.xyz/api-and-sdk/json-rpc-methods) for the call parameters.
